---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('justuno')!;
const path = '/apps/justuno';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/justuno');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/justuno');

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Justuno an email marketing platform?',
    answer: 'Evaluate it for onsite list growth and verify the current sending scope separately. Demonstrate the receiving ESP integration before assigning lifecycle jobs.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Justuno vs Privy?',
    answer: 'Compare the same form, preference mapping, targeting and mobile workflow in both products. No comparative speed or feature winner is established.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Quiz data to ESP?',
    answer: 'Sync tags and custom properties — verify mapping day one for welcome branching.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Pricing drivers?',
    answer: 'Obtain current traffic, feature and service terms and include the receiving sender and integration maintenance.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Justuno replace Klaviyo?',
    answer: 'Use the required lifecycle journeys as acceptance cases. This review evaluates capture and does not establish full sender replacement coverage.',
  },
  {
    question: 'AI recommendations?',
    answer: 'Demonstrate the required recommendation block and current plan support. If a sender uses its output, verify SKU availability and permission at dispatch.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Biggest mistake?',
    answer: 'Enabling capture before permission, destination fields, purchase exits and queue ownership have been verified.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Migration handoff?',
    answer: 'Validate the destination before cutover with outbound sends disabled. Map quiz fields and channel permission separately, transfer suppressions, cancel old queued work and assign one sender per purpose. Set timing from measured ingestion and cancellation tests.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Beauty brand fit?',
    answer: 'A preference quiz can inform education content if the field mapping, current permission and safe fallback paths work.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/apps" class="text-sm font-bold text-[#9a5b16] hover:text-[#24170f]">← All tool reviews</a>
      <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Onsite capture evaluation</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Justuno positions its current product around onsite list growth, popups and visitor identification. Evaluate the capture-to-sender handoff before assigning it a role in your Shopify stack. Preference collection, permission evidence and downstream welcome routing are separate jobs; demonstrate the installed integration rather than assuming a named ESP receives every field.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#5d3a1d]">The skincare, outdoor-gear and product-release examples below are proposed evaluation cases, not deployments we performed. Use them to inspect form behavior, missing fields, duplicate submissions and the receiving sender before enabling live follow-up.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#5d3a1d]">Availability checked November 25, 2026: the <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/justuno-pop-ups-email-conversion">Shopify listing</a> currently says the app is unavailable. <a class="link" href="https://www.justuno.com/">Justuno’s website</a> still markets popups, Spotlight and list growth. Confirm a supported Shopify installation and integration route directly before planning a new deployment; listing status alone does not establish that existing accounts stopped working.</p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps/privy">Privy review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox
      title="Verdict: Justuno for Shopify"
      picks={[
        { label: 'Role', tool: 'Capture layer', reason: 'Evaluate popup and preference capture, then verify the receiving sender.' },
        { label: 'Strength', tool: 'Quiz funnels', reason: 'Shade, fit, and collection interest tagging at opt-in.' },
        { label: 'Pricing', tool: 'Current quote', reason: 'Match traffic, features, services and paired sender costs.' },
        { label: 'Pairing', tool: 'Sequenzy / Klaviyo', reason: 'Verify destination integration and welcome field mapping.' },
        { label: 'Mistake', tool: 'ESP replacement', reason: 'Demonstrate every required sender job before consolidation.' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Capture intelligence before the ESP takes over</h2>
      <p>For a skincare quiz, map concern and routine preferences into explicit fields, then preview the corresponding welcome content with sends disabled. Test unanswered questions, changed answers and an unknown value. Use a safe fallback rather than routing an incomplete profile into a specific recommendation. Compare purchasers and contribution against an appropriate control; no first-purchase lift is documented.</p>
      <p>Proposed outdoor-gear test: compare a trail-running bundle offer on Instagram landing pages with a layering-guide lead magnet on SEO content. Randomize eligible visitors within each traffic source rather than comparing inherently different audiences. Measure purchasers and contribution after discounts, capture fees and downstream sends; no 22% acquisition-cost reduction is established.</p>
      <p>Before treating a capture tool as your campaign system, inventory welcome, cart, replenishment and winback requirements. Ask which system owns each trigger, purchase exit, suppression update and queue. Demonstrate those paths with the current product; this review does not establish a basic Justuno sender or a revenue outcome from adding another platform.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Feature depth and Shopify sync</h2>
      <p>
        Evaluate current support for smart popups, A/B testing, gamification, onsite product recommendations and behavior rules against your required plan. Test whether the selected Shopify-to-ESP integration transfers each tag and property, including missing values, before enabling welcome branches.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Best deployments:</strong> Quiz-to-welcome pipelines, collection-specific exit intent, traffic-source offer testing, cart saver bars feeding SMS and email lists simultaneously.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Limits:</strong> Confirm current email-sending and lifecycle capabilities with the supplier. Downstream reporting needs consistent identifiers and attribution windows across the handoff; UTM parameters alone cannot establish causal revenue lift.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing versus Privy and ROI math</h2>
      <p>Obtain current quotes for the required traffic, features, services and receiving ESP. Reproduce the same popup and preference-mapping brief in Justuno and Privy, including mobile behavior and operator effort. Neither a historical starting price nor a feature label establishes which stack costs less.</p>
      <p>Model cost per acquired purchaser alongside popup conversion. As an illustrative calculation, 4.2% opt-in followed by 11% purchase gives 0.462% purchasers per exposed visitor; 7% opt-in followed by 3% purchase gives 0.21%. These are hypothetical rates, not measured results, and neither proves incrementality without a comparable randomized control and matched costs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Four proposed deployment tests on Shopify</h2>
      <p><strong>1. Skincare quiz — sender handoff.</strong> Submit complete and partial answers, inspect the destination properties and preview the correct welcome branch. Keep preference data separate from email permission; no purchase improvement is claimed.</p>
      <p><strong>2. Traffic-source popups — outdoor gear.</strong> Proposed test: randomize offers within Instagram and SEO cohorts, holding exposure rules and purchase windows constant. Compare contribution per eligible visitor after offer costs rather than claiming a measured acquisition-cost reduction.</p>
      <p><strong>3. Sender responsibility — general store.</strong> Inventory lifecycle jobs before consolidating tools. Demonstrate the chosen sender receiving events and cancelling recovery after purchase; do not infer automation coverage from a capture dashboard.</p>
      <p><strong>4. Cart saver bar — vinyl shop.</strong> Proposed test: evaluate a capture bar before a release with a comparable control, frequency caps and separate channel permission. Track eligible visitor exposure, net new subscribers and purchasers; no 28% list-growth result is documented.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Newsletters and lifecycle handoff contract</h2>
      <p>Verify current sending and integration capabilities rather than assuming a basic campaign sender is available. For the selected ESP, define a measurable capture-to-ingestion target from testing, map quiz properties separately from channel permission, and assign welcome and cart sends to named owners. Replayed events must not enqueue duplicates; recheck purchase and suppression state when a message is dispatched and cancel stale queued work. A universal sixty-second handoff is not established.</p>
      <p>Order and shipping notifications require their own event and sender inventory. Quiz capture does not authorize promotional content in a transactional message. Keep necessary service notices distinct from welcome and cart marketing, and document which system owns each notification.</p>
      <p>Connect and validate the destination ESP before enabling its outbound workflows. Compare ingestion with sends disabled, transfer suppression and permission evidence, then cancel old queued work before switching ownership. Set the cutover date from successful tests and staffing rather than a universal same-week requirement.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ledger-card mb-12">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Integration checklist</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Justuno plus ESP operating contract</h2>

      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Map quiz output fields to ESP custom properties before traffic</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Assign welcome sending to one ESP; test ingestion latency, deduplication and current permission before dispatch</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Use consistent UTM parameters for downstream attribution; use randomized controls to assess incremental purchases</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Review quiz questions when the catalog changes, with a named owner and tested field mappings</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Verify recovery capabilities and name one queue owner; cancel stale work after purchase or suppression changes</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">A/B testing popups without destroying trust</h2>
      <p>Proposed outdoor-gear experiment: compare exit intent with scroll-depth triggers within each page template. A 65% scroll trigger is an illustrative variant, not a proven winner. Keep frequency, offers and eligible audiences comparable; use purchaser contribution and capture friction alongside opt-in rate. No aggregate 14% conversion lift is established.</p>
      <p>For a poster-print shop, test spin-to-win against a quiz path while keeping incentive costs visible. Higher opt-in can coexist with fewer purchasers or deeper discounts. Compare randomized cohorts over the same purchase window and include capture, messaging and discount costs; the claimed 22% opt-in lift and 6% versus 14% purchase rates are not documented observations.</p>
      <p>For mobile product pages, test reachable buttons, readable overlays and shorter forms against the desktop experience. A three-question mobile quiz and seven-question desktop quiz are possible variants, not universal limits. If later questions are requested by email, verify permission and explain their purpose; no 38% versus 12% completion result is established.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Justuno pricing and traffic tier discipline</h2>
      <p>Before an influencer promotion or vinyl release, obtain the current traffic-counting rules and tier terms. Model a hypothetical fourfold traffic spike, overages, billing period and downgrade timing alongside the baseline month. The earlier $49-to-$89 eight-day upgrade story is not a verified merchant event or current quote.</p>
      <p>At renewal, compare a simple exit-intent offer with the actual cost and effort of three quiz funnels and traffic-source rules. Obtain matched current quotes for traffic, features and support; include the paired ESP, integration work and messaging. A historical $30 starting price alone cannot establish which stack costs less.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Pros</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          {app.strengths.map((s) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">+</span>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Cons</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          {app.limits.map((l) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">−</span>{l}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="ledger-card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Who should buy</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Quiz or shade/fit capture feeding ESP welcome branches</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Traffic-source-specific offer testing at scale</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>AI on-site recommendations plus list growth</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Required targeting and preference workflows demonstrated in the selected plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Who should skip</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Need one system to demonstrate all required lifecycle jobs</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Low order volume — evaluate capture needs and total stack costs before adding complexity</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>No receiving sender verified yet — resolve ownership before launch</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Simple exit intent only — compare maintenance effort before adding complexity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Compare alternatives</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Related Shopify email tools</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg font-bold">
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/privy">Privy review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series guide</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Beauty brands</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v6 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Enterprise Justuno for multi-brand Shopify</h2><p>For a multi-brand beauty portfolio, verify account separation and namespace brand-specific quiz properties before a shared ESP receives events. Test the same customer email across two brands: permission for one brand must not silently enable another welcome sequence. Confirm supported workspaces and integration boundaries with the supplier rather than assuming campaign separation provides isolation.</p><p>To evaluate onsite recommendations, randomize eligible visitors and measure product-page conversion and total contribution separately from downstream email attribution. UTM-tagged clicks can describe a path but do not establish that email caused an onsite gain. No 8% lift or merchant deployment is documented here.</p><p>Annual renewal review: export list growth source report, quiz completion rates, cost per purchaser by capture variant. Kill underperforming spin wheel if quiz path delivers better purchasers at lower opt-in — vanity metrics hide capture stack waste.</p></div></section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v4 -->
  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Quiz funnel analytics that matter</h2>
      <p>Proposed skincare funnel analysis: record eligible quiz exposures, completions, permitted subscriptions and purchases over a predefined window such as 21 days. Use consistent denominators when comparing a quiz with a spin wheel; include discounts and stack costs. The earlier 41%, 17%, 8% and 4% rates are unsupported, and observed purchase differences would still need a control to establish causal lift.</p>
      <p>For outdoor-gear traffic, test a layering-system quiz on SEO pages and a product-interest quiz on Instagram landing pages. Compare variants within each source; source mix can explain apparent differences. Set the observation period from traffic and uncertainty, rather than asserting a three-week win.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v5 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">ESP handoff SLA</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Define and test an ESP sync target</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">For a proposed quiz-to-sender check, record submission, ingestion and queue timestamps using a stable test identifier. Retry a failed delivery and replay the same submission; confirm a single eligible welcome job. Define latency and alert thresholds from business needs and measured behavior. Verify the actual destination integration, including any connector, rather than assuming a native Sequenzy route.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v7 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Compliance</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Consent logging for quizzes</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">For a quiz permission audit, retain the displayed notice, purpose, channel, source, timestamp and withdrawal state where applicable, with a named record owner. Quiz answers alone are not marketing permission. Verify export, correction and deletion behavior across the capture tool and ESP; supplier support, legal applicability and response deadlines require separate confirmation. No completed GDPR request or twenty-four-hour fulfillment is documented.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v8 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Justuno support and theme conflicts</h2><p>Proposed theme regression check: inspect mobile overlay stacking, keyboard access, close controls and opt-in submission in a staging theme before deployment. Record script placement and the responsible integration owner for agency handoffs. A two-day revenue dip and support resolution are not documented events.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v9 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">ROI</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Capture cost per purchaser</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">For a skincare capture-cost comparison, calculate cost per acquired purchaser over matched randomized cohorts and a declared attribution window. Include traffic acquisition, capture fees, ESP fees, sends, discounts and implementation effort. The $4.20 versus $7.80 comparison and finance approval after sixty days are unsupported; retire variants using measured contribution and uncertainty rather than opt-in alone.</p><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Document Justuno variant winners in shared ops doc — quarterly review prevents stale popup rules after catalog refresh.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="ledger-card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Ops rhythm</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Weekly capture review</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">A suggested weekly capture review can cover opt-in by page template, purchaser conversion by variant, permission failures, duplicate events and ESP ingestion delay. Assign an owner and escalation path, and reconcile exports where available. A fifteen-minute meeting is a planning example, not evidence that the current dashboard covers every operational check.</p></div></section>

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Capture is upstream of every email tool on this site</h2>
      <p>Treat capture and lifecycle sending as separate responsibilities and verify current Justuno capabilities before assigning either role. For a mechanical-keyboard shop, switch-preference answers could inform tactile versus linear welcome content in Klaviyo, subject to valid email permission. Test field mapping, duplicate submissions, withdrawal and purchase-state changes. Do not infer higher clicks or lower profile costs from collecting more quiz data; those require a matched measurement plan.</p>
      <p>When comparing Privy with Justuno, reproduce the actual exit-intent, countdown, quiz and traffic-source rules your team needs. For outdoor gear, a layering-system quiz on SEO content and a single-product offer on Instagram are proposed use cases. Validate current features, operating effort and purchaser contribution rather than asserting a proven channel winner.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Three capture scenarios with ESP pairing</h2>
      <p><strong>Scenario A — Specialty coffee, capture plus a verified sender.</strong> A brew-method quiz could feed pour-over versus espresso education. Map stable answer values rather than presentation labels, test a changed preference and inspect the receiving profile before dispatch. Verify the selected integration and current permission; cancel recovery after a purchase. Compare purchaser contribution across randomized variants without assuming sync speed or a quiz cost advantage.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario B — Board game publisher, Justuno plus Klaviyo.</strong> Illustrative workflow: map pre-order interest and backer-versus-retail preference into distinct properties. A backer tag is not a channel permission record. Test retail-promotion exclusions, current order state and queued-message cancellation, with an owner for exceptions; no measured support-cost saving is established.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario C — Camping gear, Justuno AI recommendations.</strong> Proposed evaluation: compare recommendation blocks against a randomized control and separate onsite conversion from email-attributed orders. If email uses a recommended SKU, verify product availability and permissions at send time. No 8% conversion lift or finance approval is established.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Workflow tests: sync speed, consent, theme conflicts</h2>
      <p><strong>Test 1 — ESP handoff SLA.</strong> Proposed check: opt in on a mobile product page, submit a duplicate event, create a cart and complete a purchase before queued recovery. Verify permission, ingestion timing, deduplication and cancellation in the sending ESP. Define a measured latency target; no twelve-minute causal threshold or 9% open-rate effect is established.</p>
      <p><strong>Test 2 — Consent metadata.</strong> Proposed check: export quiz permission evidence and reconcile it with the ESP, then withdraw email permission and verify suppression before dispatch. Preserve the notice and its version alongside purpose, channel and source. No completed legal request or twenty-four-hour fulfillment is documented.</p>
      <p><strong>Test 3 — Theme z-index regression.</strong> Proposed check: inspect the popup across supported mobile viewports after a staging theme update. Verify stacking, dismissal, form submission and integration events; document script placement, the integration owner and escalation path. No observed outage or support resolution is established.</p>
      <p><strong>Test 4 — Variant winner kill switch.</strong> Proposed check: reconcile opt-in, purchaser conversion and contribution by randomized capture variant. Specify an observation window and stopping rule before reviewing outcomes. Disable losing variants and confirm they no longer display; no sixty-day finance decision is documented.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Buyer checklist before Justuno annual renewal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>ESP paired, permission mapped and ingestion meeting a measured latency target?</li>
        <li>Traffic-source-specific popups outperform site-wide single offer?</li>
        <li>Quiz or fit capture feeding welcome branches with measurable click lift?</li>
        <li>Capture review scheduled at an appropriate cadence with named queue, integration and escalation owners?</li>
        <li>Permission records exportable and reconcilable across capture and ESP, with a named owner and applicable obligations separately confirmed?</li>
        <li>Underperforming capture variants killed — not left running for opt-in vanity?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Choose the capture layer and sender together from demonstrated requirements. Validate preference mapping, permission updates, replay handling and queue ownership in the intended integration. Compare the same brief with <a class="link" href="/apps/privy">Privy</a>; this review establishes no targeting, operating-speed or downstream platform winner.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold">
      <a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify email tools →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparison hub →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/use-cases/segmentation">Segmentation guide →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Justuno Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
